import sys
sys.dont_write_bytecode=True
import additional_pfp_domain_remaining_audit as a
a.record('pfp/domain/ports/exact_ports.py',1,171,'Read every exact arithmetic/homology/holonomy/functional/pharmacy/digest/retraction protocol. Runtime-checkable annotations describe method presence, not correctness or certificate verification. Functional evaluation takes exact Fraction matrices/residual but domain laws remain caller/implementation obligations. Global retraction injection can fall back to a homology object based only on retraction_turn presence, without checking loop method, and suppresses all exceptions during fallback. Such lookup may turn dependency defects into unavailable-port behavior; no computation or proof is supplied by the interfaces themselves.',['protocol vs proof','injected computation','weak fallback capability check','error hiding'])
a.record('pfp/domain/homology/carrier.py',1,85,'Read declared proto-support booleans, directed edge, bounds and carrier. ProtoSupport is a seven-flag admission defaulting to true, not evidence of ontological support. Edge checks exact integer endpoints but permits negatives/self-loops. Carrier checks only counts and endpoint membership; it does not require unique/integer vertices, distinct edges, full support or a simplicial complex. StaticCellBounds has no constructor validation, ignores max_budget in check_bounds and permits negative supplied counts. Tuple annotations/frozen records do not freeze accepted lists. These are limited data invariants rather than a derivation or complete carrier certificate.',['declared support','partial carrier invariants','budget not enforcement','shallow frozen data'])
a.record('pfp/domain/homology/cochain.py',1,162,'Read matrix shape/type checks, chain/cochain pairing, transpose and result records. Exact-int excludes bool and rational permits only int/Fraction. Pairing checks dimension and vector length. BoundaryMatrix.transpose loses shape for any0-by-n input by returning0-by-0 rather than n-by-0; this is a concrete empty-dimension algebra defect to probe. Frozen dataclasses retain caller mutable sequence inputs. SmithNormalFormResult carries no check of U*A*V, unimodularity, divisibility/rank or shape; DualCertificate carries no validation of residuals, feasible flags or gap. They must remain untrusted records until a caller recomputes the obligations.',['matrix shape','empty dimension transpose','exact pairing','unchecked decomposition certificate'])
a.record('pfp/domain/homology/ddc.py',1,74,'Read eight declared primitive labels, step record and tape summaries. Delta is carrier-size subtraction; only cost/final fuel nonnegativity is checked, without exact integer or carrier/index/obstruction validation. Contractiveness compares each stored obstruction pair but does not bind successive states. Fuel conservation checks initial minus total costs against only the last fuel, and empty tapes return true even without initial-fuel validation. PASS is an unconstrained default status. These summaries do not certify per-step resource conservation, replay continuity or actual primitive semantics.',['primitive labels','endpoint-only fuel accounting','tape continuity absent','passive status'])
a.record('pfp/domain/homology/qddc.py',1,154,'Read strict Pydantic wire models and port. Rational strings must round-trip through Fraction with text/bit limits; dimensions and collection sizes are bounded and operator real/imag parts square/matched. State cochain length matches adjacent differential row/column counts. Hermiticity, d-next*d-prev zero, positivity, trace, projector/idempotence/unitarity, probability range and consistency of Hodge/result components are intentionally delegated to native constructors and not checked here. Request/result types alone cannot attest the mathematical result. This is a documented syntax/shape boundary, with no native execution in this review.',['bounded wire syntax','shape validation','native math trust','operator vs density'])
a.record('pfp/domain/homology/cycle_balance.py',1,240,'Read quartet vocabulary, carrier/problem constructor and candidate declaration. Strict fields exclude unknowns/coercion and validate edge IDs, irreflexivity, endpoint/face references, matrix dimensions, d1*d2=0, z in ker d1 and supplied d1z equality. No link from d1 entries to declared oriented edges or d2 entries to face boundaries is checked here; duplicate vertices/face IDs and repeated minus prefixes remain possible. Candidate fields are explicitly untrusted claims, appropriately not self-certifying. to_domain tuple-converts sequences and maps exact nominal values, introducing further owner dependencies. Dataclass/model frozen status does not freeze list contents.',['chain law validation','incidence/source binding','untrusted candidate','wire conversion'])
a.record('pfp/domain/homology/cycle_balance.py',241,427,'Read verifier/receipt/quartet conversion and digest checks. Verifier checks nonempty unique declared rule labels, not their execution or required rule completeness. UNVERIFIED receipts must omit verdict data; VERIFIED receipts need no nonnull witness here. Claim-hygiene strings and hashes are metadata, not proofs. check_digest_bindings compares model digest references with separately supplied raw objects and recomputes a receipt digest with an empty digest field; it does not establish that raw objects equal the model content or that verification occurred. The explicit bytes-not-verification docstring is accurate. Need aggregate/verifier callers before asserting a complete acceptance path.',['receipt state boundary','rule labels vs execution','raw/model binding','digest not verification'])
a.report()
